      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "mkinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T22:39:35Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim): simulate and verify external NC programs against the setup\n\nAdd camcraft_app::nc_sim. It takes a program that camcraft-gcode parsed\nand simulates it against the setup:\n- maps each T number to cutter geometry (an explicit map, the document's\n  tool numbers, or a .camtools row) and refuses unmapped numbers by name;\n- maps program coordinates to world millimetres (origin + sign * program,\n  with the WCS flip and the machine's inverted axes; arcs reverse sense\n  when one in-plane axis is negated);\n- cuts the setup stock with the dexel engine and measures the deviation\n  from the target model; refuses a setup with no stock by name;\n- runs verify::solid_hits, bands_vs_fixtures_held and\n  rapids_vs_fixtures_held, and the machine travel, feed, spindle and tool\n  size limits, each finding on its 1-based NC line;\n- builds a PlaySeed (PlaySeed::of_planned) so the playback can run it.\n\ncamcraft-app now depends on camcraft-gcode; the decision record is\ndocs/decisions/2218-nc-sim-runner.md.\n\nFixes #2218\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
